course: dictionary
lesson: 2583
title: Dengue: a word from health and science
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «Mosquitoes can spread diseases such as West Nile virus and dengue in some places, so spray, long sleeves and nets matter.» The sentence puts dengue in a list of diseases and says mosquitoes spread them, so dengue must be an illness.
explain: The other clues help too. "In some places" tells you dengue is not found everywhere. Spray, long sleeves and nets are things people use to stop mosquito bites, so dengue must be something you can catch from a bite.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Mosquitoes can spread diseases such as West Nile virus and an illness that..." It still makes sense, so you are on the right track. For the exact details, such as the symptoms, the dictionary gives the full answer.
fact: Dengue is a disease, spread by the bite of certain mosquitoes.
fact: Dengue can cause a high fever, a headache and very painful muscles and joints.
fact: «Dengue fever» is another name for dengue.
fact: A «dengue outbreak» is when many people catch dengue in one place at the same time.
fact: Dengue is a noun that you cannot count, so you do not say "a dengue" or "three dengues".
exercise: «Mosquitoes can spread diseases such as West Nile virus and dengue in some places.» What is dengue? | A sort of insect spray | A type of tropical fruit | A kind of mosquito net | *A tropical disease spread by mosquito bites
exercise: Which of these is a symptom of dengue? | Sunburn | Hiccups | Itchy eyes | *High fever
exercise: Which words in the sentence show that dengue is not found everywhere? | long sleeves | matter | spread | *in some places
test: Why do people remove standing water where mosquitoes breed? | To make the rain fall faster | To make the garden look tidy | To give mosquitoes somewhere to swim | *To stop mosquitoes breeding
test: Which phrase is correct English? | a dengues | the dengue are | *dengue fever | many dengues
exam: Why do people use nets, repellent and long sleeves in places with dengue? | *To stop mosquitoes biting them | To keep their feet warm | To make themselves look smart | To help a fever go up
